---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About ZeroJS"
	description="The story and philosophy behind ZeroJS — a commitment to hyper-fast, accessible, and durable web craftsmanship."
	pubDate={new Date('October 12 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<h2>The Mission</h2>
	<p>
		The modern web has grown bloated. In recent years, simple content websites routinely ship multiple megabytes of client-side JavaScript bundles just to display text and images. This trend leads to sluggish load times on mobile networks, degraded battery life, fragile hydration mismatches, and unnecessary barriers to accessibility.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>ZeroJS</strong> was founded as a design statement and technical manifesto: web content should be fast, accessible, and resilient by default. By eliminating unnecessary client-side JavaScript from static pages, we return to the core strengths that made the open web great.
	</p>

	<h2>Why Zero JavaScript?</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Instant First Paint:</strong> Browsers parse and paint pure HTML and CSS faster than any runtime can execute. Zero JavaScript means your content appears without the "white screen of death" or layout shifts.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Unbreakable Reliability:</strong> Content rendered with standard HTML doesn't break if a third-party script fails to load, a network connection drops mid-bundle, or a browser disables JavaScript.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Global Accessibility:</strong> Low-spec devices and cellular networks around the world can view and navigate ZeroJS without lag or heavy battery drain.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Carbon & Energy Efficiency:</strong> Transmitting less data and running fewer CPU cycles directly reduces energy consumption on both servers and client devices.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>The Architecture</h2>
	<p>
		ZeroJS is powered by modern web tooling, deliberately configured for maximum performance:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Astro 7+</strong> — For blazing-fast static site compilation and component-driven authoring.</li>
		<li><strong>Native CSS</strong> — Modular design tokens and CSS custom properties with zero runtime style overhead.</li>
		<li><strong>Type-Safe Content Collections</strong> — Markdown and MDX authoring with strict schema validation.</li>
		<li><strong>Automatic Image Optimization</strong> — Next-gen responsive WebP formats generated at compile time.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Open Web Standards</h2>
	<p>
		We believe in the open web. ZeroJS is fully syndication-friendly with native RSS feeds, semantic HTML5 tags, standard sitemaps, and zero vendor lock-in.
	</p>
	<p>
		Feel free to explore our <a href="/blog">writings</a>, subscribe to our <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>, or inspect the project repository on GitHub.
	</p>
</Layout>
